      "footnote_refs": [],
      "footnote_texts": {},
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "text": "UAE labour laws apply in UAE free zones, with the exception of the Dubai International Financial Centre (DIFC) and the Abu Dhabi Global Market (ADGM). The DIFC and ADGM have developed their own labour regulations, which include specific provisions regarding the termination of employment contracts and the payment of compensation. \n\nAccording to clarifications issued by the ADGM and the DIFC, unemployment insurance for employees registered in these zones is voluntary. For employees in other free zones, a general procedure requiring mandatory insurance applies.",
      "formatted_text": [
        {
